<ArticleLayout slug="meta-tiktok-against-douyin-rednote" ctaLabel="Build the campaign for both" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">Meta and TikTok print their ad specs where anyone can read them. Douyin and RedNote do not. Set the four side by side and a Western 9:16 cut survives the frame. What it runs into next is a safe zone that leaks by a few dozen pixels, and a cover nobody on the Western side asked for.</p>

  <h2>How do you adapt TikTok ads for Douyin?</h2>

  <p>Keep the 9:16 master and rebuild the export. On the published record the frame survives, Meta's safe zone leaks a few dozen pixels on Douyin, a 9-second TikTok cut is too short for Douyin TopView, and RedNote needs a 3:4 cover the Western build never made. hubStudio plans that capture as a single shoot day.</p>

  <h2>How to read these numbers</h2>

  <p>These specs are not read from a creator backend. Douyin's creator and advertiser surfaces serve no specification text to anyone not logged in. Neither do RedNote's creator, advertiser and help surfaces, the help center of its Juguang ad platform included. So no open source reaches the official value for either app. The one readable exception, Douyin's upload API documentation, is named below.</p>

  <p>What follows is the most commonly published figure for each Douyin and RedNote spec, collected across three separate collections of 12, 17 and 20 independent sources in Chinese and English on 10 September 2026, with the number of sources that agreed shown per row. Counts from different collections are never added together. Rows marked consensus had broad agreement. Rows marked contested did not, and those carry the full spread rather than a single number.</p>

  <p>Treat this as the best available public reading, not as the rule. Platform specs change without announcement and often without an English notice at all. Before you build a batch to any number on this page, open your own creator account and confirm it there. Reviewed 15 September 2026.</p>

  <p>The Meta and TikTok half is different. Meta's Facebook Ads Guide serves one undated page per placement under the Awareness objective, and TikTok's ads help center prints a month on each page: auction in-feed (June 2026), reservation in-feed (July 2025), TopView (June 2026) and creative best practices (June 2025). Every one of them was read logged out on 10 September 2026 and again on 15 September. Those rows are primary readings for the placement, objective or buying type named, and for nothing else. Douyin's Open Platform documentation for its upload API is readable too, and its row says it covers the API route only.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">RedNote's advertising help surfaces served no advertising specification text to an unauthenticated request on 10 September 2026, or again on 15 September. That covers the Juguang ad platform, its help center, a help document, its API documentation and the help center of its creator marketplace. Between them they returned page titles, a login page, a chatbot prompt, an empty-article notice and an API onboarding note, and no creative spec. The RedNote rows on this page therefore cover organic note formats only.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: five direct unauthenticated fetches of RedNote-owned advertising and creator-marketplace surfaces, 10 September 2026 and again 15 September 2026, response content recorded per request. Primary observation, not a specification.</p>

  <h2>Meta, TikTok, Douyin and RedNote ad specs side by side</h2>

  <p>Six rows a producer briefs from. The Meta and TikTok cells say what the page says. The Douyin and RedNote cells give the most commonly published figure, the number of sources that agreed, and whether the row is consensus or contested. No cell mixes two apps.</p>

