  <p>Three of those rows decide the shoot. Duration first.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">One cut length fits every duration figure used here except Douyin's open screen: 10 to 60 seconds. TikTok's reservation and TikTok TopView formats stop at 60. Douyin TopView starts at 10, so a 9-second cut, the short end of TikTok's own recommendation, is too short to reuse there. Open screen shows a video for 5 seconds and needs its own cut.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: TikTok ads help center reservation and TopView pages read 10 and 15 September 2026 (primary), and Douyin paid-ad figures from 5 Douyin-specific sources collected 10 September 2026 (modal). Derived by intersecting the published ranges.</p>

  <p>Then the cover, which is where the Western build fails RedNote outright.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Neither Meta's video ad pages nor TikTok's in-feed pages set a cover image. RedNote's most commonly published cover is a 3:4 frame at 1080 by 1440 pixels, so a Western cut arrives without the asset RedNote shows first. A centered 3:4 cut of a 1080 by 1920 frame measures exactly 1080 by 1440, which makes the cover a moment to plan on set rather than a crop to find later.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Meta and TikTok specification pages read in full on 10 and 15 September 2026 (primary, absence), and RedNote cover figures from 20 sources collected 10 September 2026 (modal). Derived; the fit is geometry.</p>

  <p>Sound runs both ways, and the table already shows it: optional on Meta, required on TikTok reservation and TikTok TopView, absent from the dated Douyin open-screen file. One sound-on master and one silent short cut cover all of it. The file row rests on the weakest input on the page, a RedNote cap that a single source publishes, and the export line in the capture plan carries that arithmetic with its label.</p>

  <h2>What do you capture once so both halves come from one shoot?</h2>

  <p>Eight decisions on set, in the order a producer meets them. Each names its input, and none is a platform requirement.</p>

