  <h2>Questions buyers ask about running one campaign on Meta, TikTok, Douyin and RedNote</h2>

  <h3>Can a TikTok ad run on Douyin?</h3>

  <p>Not as the same ad. The apps run separate accounts and separate ad platforms. The 9:16 frame carries over. What needs checking is the duration window, since the most commonly published Douyin TopView starts at 10 seconds, the safe zone, where no Douyin figure agrees, and the sound rule on the dated open-screen format. Rebuild the export from the master, not from the TikTok file.</p>

  <h3>Are Douyin and TikTok ad specs the same?</h3>

  <p>No. TikTok publishes its specs, and its TopView runs 5 to 60 seconds. The most commonly published Douyin TopView runs 10 to 60, on 4 of 5 Douyin-specific sources. TikTok bans plain white in the first 3 seconds because of its logo, and no Douyin source prints that rule. TikTok's safe zone is a downloadable template. Douyin's is a contested set of pixel figures.</p>

  <h3>What changes when a Meta campaign moves to RedNote?</h3>

  <p>The cover. Meta's video ad pages set no cover. RedNote shows a 3:4 cover first, 1080 by 1440 on 13 of 20 published sources, with a center square lifted into the profile grid. A 4:5 Feed cut crops to 3:4 with 45 pixels lost on each side. RedNote's ad documentation is not readable logged out, so these are organic note figures.</p>

  <h3>How do TikTok and Douyin safe zones differ?</h3>

  <p>TikTok publishes no inset. Its help pages say the safe zone shrinks with caption length and supply template files instead, and every TikTok pixel figure in circulation is third-party. Douyin has no official figure either, and the published Chinese insets span 220 to 288 pixels at the top and 200 to 380 at the bottom. Build to the largest, then check the TikTok template.</p>

  <h3>How do I shoot one campaign for Western and Chinese platforms?</h3>

  <p>Shoot one 9:16 master with critical content inside a box from 108 to 972 pixels across and 420 to 1248 down on a 1080 by 1920 frame. Plan a cut of 10 to 60 seconds and a cut of 5. Land the proposition by second 3 without a white open, mix sound on stems, and hold a 3:4 cover moment. One shoot day, two exports.</p>
